<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Connections on Layer5 Documentation</title><link>/tags/connections/</link><description>Recent content in Connections on Layer5 Documentation</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><atom:link href="/tags/connections/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Manage Environments</title><link>/cloud/guides/workspaces/managing-environments/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/cloud/guides/workspaces/managing-environments/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;An environment groups connections into a deploy target and is the means by which a workspace exposes those connections to its teams. This guide covers every task on an environment. For the model behind it, read the &lt;a href="/cloud/concepts/environments/"&gt;Environments concept&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
