&lt;p&gt;The feature matrix lists environments under the Enterprise plan. Layer5 Cloud does not refuse environment actions because of the plan.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Meshery Server Registration</title><link>/cloud/concepts/meshery-server-registration/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/cloud/concepts/meshery-server-registration/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Layer5 Cloud is a &lt;a href="https://docs.meshery.io/extensibility/providers"&gt;Meshery remote provider&lt;/a&gt;. When a Meshery Server uses Layer5 Cloud, hosted or self-hosted, the server registers itself with Cloud on behalf of the signed-in user. Registration is what makes that Meshery Server known to Cloud: it appears as a &lt;code&gt;meshery&lt;/code&gt; connection owned by that user. This page explains what the server sends, how Cloud tells a new server from one it already knows, what survives re-registration, and what each failure means.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>